mail.com","name":"cjakabos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-28T13:49:50Z","email":"csaba.jakabos@gmail.com","name":"cjakabos"},"message":"Remove the obsolete Umami bootstrap helper and align the repo docs and\nnightly setup with the current dedicated Umami database/service design.\n\nWhat changed:\n- deleted scripts/bootstrap-umami-db.sh\n- removed the bootstrap-umami-db target from the Makefile\n- updated README.md to start Umami with the dedicated services directly:\n  umami-portfolio-db and umami-portfolio\n- updated docs/umami-analytics.md to document the direct startup flow\n  instead of the old bootstrap step\n- removed the nightly workflow step that invoked the deleted bootstrap\n  script\n\nWhy:\nThe repository no longer uses the older design where Umami shared the main\nPostgreSQL instance and required a separate database/role bootstrap step.\nThe current compose setup provisions a dedicated Umami Postgres service that\ncreates its own database and role automatically, so the bootstrap script had\nbecome stale and misleading.","tree":{"sha":"7a4461ebd9acd1fc40d2fdded904561360d45b7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cjakabos/portfolio-web/git/trees/7a4461ebd9acd1fc40d2fdded904561360d45b7e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cjakabos/portfolio-web/git/commits/fbb35b0ee19708f9bfc09f8e83b59dde85ebad55","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54838312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cjakabos","id":54838312,"login":"cjakabos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODM4MzEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cjakabos/portfolio-web/commit/fbb35b0ee19708f9bfc09f8e83b59dde85ebad55","node_id":"C_kwDOGVz28doAKGZiYjM1YjBlZTE5NzA4ZjliZmMwOWY4ZTgzYjU5ZGRlODVlYmFkNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cjakabos/portfolio-web/commit/f47babb56c1a2a07431d2227c6cc40edb6c5ffc8","sha":"f47babb56c1a2a07431d2227c6cc40edb6c5ffc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cjakabos/portfolio-web/commits/f47babb56c1a2a07431d2227c6cc40edb6c5ffc8"}],"sha":"fbb35b0ee19708f9bfc09f8e83b59dde85ebad55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cjakabos/portfolio-web/commits/fbb35b0ee19708f9bfc09f8e83b59dde85ebad55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54838312?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cjakabos","id":54838312,"login":"cjakabos","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODM4MzEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjakabos","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cjakabos/portfolio-web/commits/f47babb56c1a2a07431d2227c6cc40edb6c5ffc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-27T16:55:33Z","email":"csaba.jakabos@gmail.com","name":"cjakabos"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-27T16:55:33Z","email":"csaba.jakabos@gmail.com","name":"cjakabos"},"message":"feat(release): add contract manifest and release discipline docs\n\nIntroduce a versioned contract snapshot manifest and the release-discipline\nartifacts that turn the remaining backlog into an executable review and\npromotion process.\n\nWhat changed:\n- added contracts/openapi/manifest.json as the governed manifest for browser-\n  facing OpenAPI snapshots, including per-service snapshot revisions, owners,\n  upstream versions, and release-critical flags\n- extended scripts/contracts/openapi_contracts.py to validate the manifest,\n  exclude it from snapshot iteration, and generate packages/contracts/src/\n  versions.ts alongside the existing TypeScript clients\n- regenerated the contracts package barrel so contract consumers can import the\n  snapshot manifest and revision metadata from @portfolio/contracts\n- added platform docs for contract release discipline, release promotion\n  criteria, the release checklist, and a dry-run example for a representative\n  governed contract change\n- updated README.md, docs/platform/README.md, and tests/README.md with the\n  new release and contract-governance references\n\nWhy:\nThe repo already had snapshot drift detection and generated clients, but it did\nnot yet version the governed snapshots or define a consistent release process\nfor gateway, auth, AI, and contract-touching changes. This commit closes that\nlast productization gap and gives reviewers a single governed path from API\nchange to generated client update to release decision.\n\nVerification:\n- python3 scripts/contracts/openapi_contracts.py generate-ts\n- python3 scripts/contracts/openapi_contracts.py generate-ts --check\n- git diff --check","tr