lfSoko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolfSoko","id":8589105,"login":"WolfSoko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1ODkxMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolfSoko/wol-sok-mono/commits/46e2cebe1d8e1aaf000ea5347166dc06a64cbcc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T06:10:11Z","email":"8589105+WolfSoko@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Wolfram Sokollek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T06:10:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deploy): use npm-safe predeploy install syntax for firebase-tools v15 (#2387)\n\nPR #2361 added `npm --prefix $RESOURCE_DIR install --omit=dev` as the\npredeploy hook, but firebase-tools'' predeploy runner pipes the whole\ncommand through cross-env-shell as a single argv element. cross-env''s\nenv-setter regex (/(\\w+)=.../, unanchored) matches \"omit=dev\" inside\nthat string, so the entire command is swallowed as an env-var\nassignment (OMIT=dev) and `command` ends up null — npm install is\nsilently never invoked, which is why the predeploy fix never worked.\n\nSwitch to npm''s documented space-separated flag form (`--omit dev`),\nwhich contains no `=` and is therefore never misparsed by cross-env''s\nregex. Verified against the actual pinned firebase-tools@15.30.2 +\ncross-env@7.0.3 source by replaying their parseCommand logic locally:\nthe old string resolves to command=null, the new one resolves to the\nfull npm command intact.\n\nCloses #2359\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WUEusWYEw8rv3WVYZFXte9\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"249761b3de9af7c87f367b8fe90ce44c2a735874","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolfSoko/wol-sok-mono/git/trees/249761b3de9af7c87f367b8fe90ce44c2a735874"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolfSoko/wol-sok-mono/git/commits/46e2cebe1d8e1aaf000ea5347166dc06a64cbcc2","verification":{"payload":"tree 249761b3de9af7c87f367b8fe90ce44c2a735874\nparent e58eb459f1c38c6d604d617db72fefcb490d8d6f\nauthor Wolfram Sokollek <8589105+WolfSoko@users.noreply.github.com> 1790662211 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790662211 +0200\n\nfix(deploy): use npm-safe predeploy install syntax for firebase-tools v15 (#2387)\n\nPR #2361 added `npm --prefix $RESOURCE_DIR install --omit=dev` as the\npredeploy hook, but firebase-tools'' predeploy runner pipes the whole\ncommand through cross-env-shell as a single argv element. cross-env''s\nenv-setter regex (/(\\w+)=.../, unanchored) matches \"omit=dev\" inside\nthat string, so the entire command is swallowed as an env-var\nassignment (OMIT=dev) and `command` ends up null — npm install is\nsilently never invoked, which is why the predeploy fix never worked.\n\nSwitch to npm''s documented space-separated flag form (`--omit dev`),\nwhich contains no `=` and is therefore never misparsed by cross-env''s\nregex. Verified against the actual pinned firebase-tools@15.30.2 +\ncross-env@7.0.3 source by replaying their parseCommand logic locally:\nthe old string resolves to command=null, the new one resolves to the\nfull npm command intact.\n\nCloses #2359\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WUEusWYEw8rv3WVYZFXte9\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu1ZDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt/oQAB6Adw3I5E8W2lrjN+RFs71+\nGLdDFjI+cY2FXKO