api.github.com/repos/WolfSoko/wol-sok-mono/commits/8e13eda4ac398fcef930a2392868f2fce2763bac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8589105?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolfSoko","id":8589105,"login":"WolfSoko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1ODkxMDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolfSoko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolfSoko/wol-sok-mono/commits/33003536143d862f32c55b5911919fee79d6961f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:16:27Z","email":"8589105+WolfSoko@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Wolfram Sokollek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:16:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(renovate): rebase when behind and group all non-major updates (#2349)\n\n98 Renovate pull requests are open and almost none of them can merge. The\ncause is a contradiction between two settings:\n\n  ruleset \"Main\"   strict_required_status_checks_policy: true\n                   -> a branch must be up to date before merging\n  renovate.json    rebaseWhen: \"conflicted\"\n                   -> Renovate only rebases on conflict, never when behind\n\nA pull request that is merely behind is therefore never rebased and never\nbecomes mergeable. Eleven of twelve sampled pull requests sit at\nmergeStateStatus BEHIND with auto-merge already armed, waiting for a rebase\nthat never comes. The twelfth is DIRTY, a real conflict. That the mechanism\nworks at all is visible in #2344, which merged on its own because it happened\nto be current at the time.\n\nrebaseWhen: \"behind-base-branch\" resolves the contradiction, but on its own it\nwould drain serially: every merge invalidates the other 97, so 97 rebases and\n97 CI runs stand between two merges. On this monorepo that is days.\n\nGrouping removes the problem instead of working around it. All non-major\nupdates travel in one pull request that keeps itself current and merges. The\nNx/Angular family is deliberately excluded - the shared preset already groups\nit as \"Nx monorepo\" and attaches nx migrate postUpgradeTasks to it, and\npulling those into a 60-package branch would put migrations where nobody\nexpects them. Verified against Renovate''s own matcher: lodash, mermaid, three,\ncore-js, vega, @types/jasmine, jsdom and firebase go into the group, while\n@angular/core, @nx/workspace, nx, typescript, zone.js, @ngrx/store,\nng-packagr and @nx-dotnet/core stay out.\n\nThe config passes renovate-config-validator. The first attempt did not: mixing\n\"*\" with negated patterns is refused, so the rule carries negations only,\nwhich Renovate reads as \"everything except these\".\n\nThe 32 major updates are untouched on purpose. They need judgement - Node 24,\nVite 8, ESLint 10, the Nx/Angular chain - and no setting merges them for us.\n\nNot changed, but worth knowing: prConcurrentLimit is 2 and has been since\nNovember 2024, yet 98 pull requests are open, so it is evidently not binding\nin this installation. If the grouped pull request does not appear after a run\nor two, that setting is the first thing to check.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Qd5fJLqwwHjyCGYxnKMvuw","tree":{"sha":"165928268549cfecbc6c19e557669be3ddc1f7cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolfSoko/wol-sok-mono/git/trees/165928268549cfecbc6c19e557669be3ddc1f7cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolfSoko/wol-sok-mono/git/commits/33003536143d862f32c55b5911919fee79d6961f","verification":{"payload":"tree 165928268549cfecbc6c19e557669be3ddc1f7cf\nparent c40c9f989720c7728c6209e96eb9b4f604e3ef4f\nauthor Wolfram Sokollek <8589105+WolfSoko@users.noreply.github.com> 1789571787 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789571787 +0200\n\nci(renovate): rebase when behind and group all non-major updates (#2349)\n\n98 Renovate pull requests are open and almost none of them can merge. The\ncause is a contradiction between two settings:\n\n  ruleset \"Main\"   strict_required_status_checks_policy: true\n                   -> a branch must be up to date before merging\n  renovate.json    rebaseWhen: \"conflicted\"\n                   -> Renovate only rebases on conflict, never when behind\n\nA pull request that is merely behind is therefore never rebased and never\nbecomes mergeable. Eleven of twelve sampled pull requests sit at\nmergeStateStatus BEHIND with auto-merge already armed, waiting for a rebase\nthat never comes. The twelfth is DIRTY, a real conflict. That the mechanism\nworks at all is visible in #2344, which merged on its own because it happened\nto be current at the time.\n\nrebaseWhen: \"behind-base-branch\" resolves the contradiction, but on its own it\nwould drain serially: every merge invalidates the other 97, so 97 rebases and\n97 CI runs stand between two merges. On this monorepo that is days.\n\nGrouping removes the problem instead of working around it. All non-major\nupdates travel in one pull request that keeps itself current and merges. The\nNx/Angular family is deliberately excluded - the shared preset already groups\nit as \"Nx monorepo\" and attaches nx migrate postUpgradeTasks to it, and\npulling those into a 60-package branch would put migrations where nobody\nexpects them. Verified against Renovate''s own matcher: lodash, mermaid, three,\ncore-js, vega, @types/jasmine, jsdom and firebase go into the group, while\n@angular/core, @nx/workspace, nx, typescript, zone.js, @ngrx/store,\nng-packagr and @nx-dotnet/core stay out.\n\nThe config passes renovate-config-validator. The first attempt did not: mixing\n\"*\" with negated patterns is refused, so the rule carries negations only,\nwhich Renovate reads as \"everything except these\".\n\nThe 32 major updates are untouched on purpose. They need judgement - Node 24,\nVite 8, ESLint 10, the Nx/Angular chain - and no setting merges them for us.\n\nNot changed, but worth knowing: prConcurrentLimit is 2 and has been since\nNovember 2024, yet 98 pull requests are open, so it is evidently not binding\nin this installation. If the grouped pull request does not appear after a run\nor two, that setting is the first thing to check.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Qd5fJLqwwHjyCGYxnKMvuw","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqrLLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbU8QAJA56NBxZXdT6fGF8ENFNv7K\nggBw83A5Jo7jjuHFMKbTXvLRf+93UXlt7EDxV38v4gUaWvZwg+/W2HKDn0zJbG8Y\nwggjzDkEsm6B7ZpNkb3+r/WSRQstRFTWeiE3wltxyv7HrydLrjAGlhSehA3jzsAV\n1Kkck5SgDluB7ST9uGdIWcgKxviP6Ow5fYiv1Uh+VA5sQHez1EE6HFlJb5Fhk+/3\nGERjgKnFv+o2AhdOXZOXQkCBYTAjIARWQpA/LiidYjr4m1Mu0hkRF9PiUWLcRWHJ\nmSdwwR0SCSMDVmtRy+2AB4zsyE0oVVKCln+re6tz0fZcx/CABoaVDOmXqwFlq1iV\nF8o2NA5tUktKIbz5lWs87bWYo80n95VyJGwISOb0/a6Ju0Z6oLlmN85sqiyCTBFT\ntlH8xWxhNXCNn+O4UHDNjA8wBv4Y3p5gUzvxFjzoQOVlF3Fpjal6dHz/U1OmMT25\nLkL62KYiAYJeM1ZaGjXBrrKJtX2Qet/3C9ataiN5LCU2v6gzKM4wtOE92nldioBa\n6neZFyRru3pxoRr428hwKbDEgA8OoQsMCzrAqX7oPgYBebe8NUEQn/VhJiYZbGL0\nOICFBc4qw+yxHdGr17X/1t1ruJ6n2OdkfMG6uiwUeKX14HRNq5G6OGw+hJGByMaL\n22uqACBr/rBbk1xqf9Z8\n=R6Qn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T15:16:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":